Comparing two values of a trait that is not a reference type (for example, under `--general-traits=datatype`) in a `decreases` clause no longer crashes the verifier (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/350). Without `--trait-rank-decreases`, such values have no decreases order: a component of that type may only stay unchanged, and a call or loop iteration that changes it reports that the decreases clause might not decrease. With `--trait-rank-decreases` they are still compared by `BoxRank`.
